# Log check for X-SALV's bot half (docs/lanes/x-salv.md, "Bots, 20 minutes"):
# three ratters, closed economy.  Run
#     tools/soak.sh --closed --ratters 3     (or eve-bots --loop escort with the economy on)
# then:
#     python3 -I tools/client-ci/server-expect.py x_salv_bots
# The lane's "wrong" list: ratters docking for "recovery" (the salvage act must
# be incidental); a hold that fills is not visible in a log and stays a human read.
#
# BOTS-EXPECT:   present \+[0-9:.]+ fit\s
# BOTS-EXPECT:   present \+[0-9:.]+ loot\s
# BOTS-EXPECT:   present \+[0-9:.]+ salvage\s
# BOTS-EXPECT:   absent  recover(y)?\b.*salvage
# SERVER-EXPECT: absent  UNANSWERED (ship\.Drop|dogmaIM)
# SERVER-EXPECT: absent  panicked at
